From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] asap7/riscv32i: what SWAP_ARITH_OPERATORS buys, beside the setting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

riscv32i already swaps adder architectures during repair. Measured at
the new 780 ps clock, to global route: the reg2reg period is 835.6 ps
with it and 943.4 ps without, 11 % shorter; with flat synthesis 791.8
and 895.7 ps. The comment records it beside the setting, so the next
change to it starts from the number.

Not upstreamed. Retires on the //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
diff --git a/flow/designs/asap7/riscv32i/config.mk b/flow/designs/asap7/riscv32i/config.mk
index 373bb22e..edc6661c 100644
--- a/flow/designs/asap7/riscv32i/config.mk
+++ b/flow/designs/asap7/riscv32i/config.mk
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ export TNS_END_PERCENT   = 100
 export CTS_CLUSTER_SIZE = 10
 export CTS_CLUSTER_DIAMETER = 50
 
+# Adder architectures swapped during repair: at 780 ps the reg2reg
+# period is 11 % shorter than with swapping off (835.6 against 943.4 ps).
 export SWAP_ARITH_OPERATORS = 1
 export OPENROAD_HIERARCHICAL = 1
 
